# Phase E (#47, flip brick B1) — the stage-0 SEED anchor.
#
# Most of krapped/ is machine-generated and ignored, BUT the deterministic TEXT output of
# a one-time libclang generation is COMMITTED as the bootstrap seed: post-B5 (libclang
# reducer deleted from in-tree krapper_gen) this module can no longer (re)parse its own
# Clang-slice headers, so it builds from this committed seed under
# -Pkpp.frontend.krapper_parse=seed.
#
# Committed (deterministic, portable): the Kotlin bindings (src/), the C++ wrapper
# (krapper_parse.cc / krapper_parse.h) and the forcing headers (KrapperForce_*.h), plus the
# discovered-instantiation manifest (requested.txt). Everything else — the compiled wrapper
# object (libkrapper_parse.a, host/LLVM-pinned), the cinterop .def (carries this checkout's
# absolute krapped path), generated.txt, fixups.json, cpp-models/, *.log — stays
# machine-generated/ignored and is regenerated at build (the .def + .a by runSeedSync, a
# plain C++ compile with no libclang parse).
/krapped/*
!/krapped/requested.txt
!/krapped/src
!/krapped/src/**
!/krapped/*.cc
!/krapped/*.h
